{"decision":"edit", "issues":[{"quote":"Throughout the flip, the thumb remains at the lower right and fingers at the top.", "problem":"In the label-side frames (t=0–2.3s) the thumb grips the lower-right rim and the slender fingers the top, but after the disc is turned over (t=2.47–2.67s) the broad nail-bearing thumb sits at the upper right and the fingertips at the bottom; the hand rotates with the disc during the flip, so the thumb does not stay at the lower right."}], "caption":"A right hand pinches a Staples CD-RW disc by its rim above a dark wooden tabletop, holding the label side toward the camera while a green Staples jewel case rests in the lower-left corner. The viewpoint and background stay fixed as the disc undergoes small, slow tilts, keeping the STAPLES CD-RW text legible while a rainbow sheen drifts across the white label surface.

The hand then tilts the disc more strongly toward the light, so the printed label washes into a bright overexposed glare and the circular outline visibly foreshortens into an ellipse. The disc passes briefly and motion-blurred nearly edge-on before continuing its slow rotation onward. Its reflective data side then fills the view, showing dark mirror-like surfaces crossed by strong, bright spectral rainbow diffraction bands.

During the flip the hand rotates, bringing the thumb to the top edge and the fingers to the bottom. The lower-left jewel case and wood-grain background do not shift, showing the change comes from disc tilt rather than camera motion.", "length_note":""}
